@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: the shape of proveo in one screen — who drives it, what it decides, where it runs
' covers: cmd/proveo/**
' covers: internal/**
' Detail lives in components.puml (same directory): every package, every edge.
' This file exists because that map answers "what is there" and a newcomer first
' needs "what is this" — so it stays small on purpose. Resist adding boxes; add
' them there instead.
' Notes here are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
' 2026-10-16: the docker+egress backend is DELETED ("Retire Docker egress";
' "Refuse without sbx"); sbx is the only backend and a host without it refuses.

title Proveo — one orchestrator, one resolved launch, one backend (sbx)

actor "Consumer\nruns an agent on their repo" as Consumer
actor "Maintainer\nbuilds and publishes images" as Maintainer

component "proveo CLI\nthe single host orchestrator" as CLI <<host>>

node "Definitions — defs/" as DEFS <<host>> {
  component "harness.manifest\nregistration + capabilities" as MANIFEST <<app>>
  component "Dockerfile · entrypoint\nsubagents · bridges" as BUILD <<app>>
}
component "proveo/* images" as IMAGES <<app>>

component "LaunchSpec\nenv · seed steps · agent argv" as LAUNCH <<app>>

node "Backend" as BACKENDS <<host>> {
  component "docker sandboxes (sbx)\nbuilt-in agent + proveo mixin" as SBX <<app>>
}
component "no sbx → refuse\n(docker+egress deleted 2026-10-16)" as DOCKER <<error>>

component "the agent, on your workspace" as AGENT <<app>>
cloud "provider APIs" as PROVIDERS <<cloud>>
component "_spec/**\nwhy each shape is what it is" as SPECS <<db>>

Consumer ARROW_MAIN CLI : proveo run <target>
Maintainer ARROW_MAIN BUILD : build · deploy
BUILD ARROW_MAIN IMAGES
MANIFEST ARROW_MAIN CLI : what this harness can do
IMAGES ARROW_MAIN BACKENDS : the image a run boots

CLI ARROW_MAIN LAUNCH : resolve once, host-side
CLI ARROW_ERROR DOCKER : host cannot run sbx
LAUNCH ARROW_MAIN SBX
BACKENDS ARROW_MAIN AGENT
AGENT ARROW_CLOUD PROVIDERS : brokered, never bare
SPECS ARROW_OPTIONAL CLI : the reasoning, not the code

note right of CLI
  **One orchestrator, and it stays on the host.**
  Mounts, the sbx Kit, credential handling and
  every prompt are decided here, so the container
  receives a posture rather than the authority to
  choose one.
end note

note bottom of LAUNCH
  **Resolved once, rendered once.** The backend is
  a rendering of host-side decisions, never a
  second place to originate them. A docker
  rendering existed until 2026-10-16.
end note

note bottom of BACKENDS
  **sbx holds the boundary.** Its network policy
  decides egress and its credential proxy holds
  the key; proveo reports the policy and adds
  only add-on reach. No Squid, no MITM.
end note

note bottom of IMAGES
  **Definitions are data, images are artifacts.**
  A harness brings a manifest, a Dockerfile and an
  entrypoint, while the choices about how a run is
  assembled stay in the CLI — so adding one never
  means adding orchestration.
end note

@enduml
